[{"n":1,"title":"Grave Robbing","artist":"leroy","year":2023,"mbid":null,"heard":true,"cover":"https://cdn2.albumoftheyear.org/600x0/album/708675-grave-robbing_2134.jpg","spotify_id":null,"spotify_url":null,"desc_lfm_album":"SoundCloud description reads: ----This should explain everything. Remember where you came from. Understand why it's gone. Her spirit is angry Back into the grave she goes---- Originally, Dariacore 3 was supposed to be the last leroy album until jane popped up with an NTS Radio set. She released grave robbing on SoundCloud right after the set ended. .","desc_lfm_artist":"There are 7 artists known as Leroy:\n\n1. The EDM side project of American artist Jane Remover, also (unofficially) known as c0ncernn. Under this alias, Remover coined the genre Dariacore with her 2021 album of the same name as well as its 2 sequels. After the release of Grave Robbing in 2023, the project was supposedly retired until 2025.\n\n2. An American artist, whose music is featured in television shows such as Scrubs and Arrested Development\n\n3.","desc_mb_album":null,"desc_mb_artist":"Leroy Anderson (1908-1975) was one of the pre-eminent composers of \"classical pops\" music. Though best known for \"Sleigh Ride\" (originally a pure instrumental) and \"Syncopated Clock\" (used as theme music for the CBS \"Late Show\" and Jeopardy), he wrote many others just as deserving of attention which are still widely played in pops concerts.\n\nNote that although his first name is spelled normally, it seems to be universally pronounced le-ROY. For more information, check out the official web page at http://www.leroy-anderson.com/ .","yt_id":"YT1k1xdGaEY","genres":[],"rym":"https://rateyourmusic.com/release/album/leroy/grave-robbing","scaruffi_rating":null,"scaruffi_note":null,"wikipedia_url":null,"aoty_user_score":null,"aoty_critic_score":83,"metacritic_score":null,"label":null},{"n":2,"title":"MIR4CLEN 2","artist":"ღDJ魔女っ娘ミラクるんღ","year":2021,"mbid":null,"heard":false,"cover":"https:/